cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "logfmt: a fast, allocation-free logfmt reader for Go"
abstract: >-
  A Go library for reading the logfmt key/value log line format. Keys and
  values are reported as sub-slices of the input, so parsing a line allocates
  nothing; lookups of one or several keys stop as soon as those keys are
  settled; and quoted values decode go-logfmt's escapes, including \uXXXX, for
  round-trip interoperability.
authors:
  - family-names: Lindvall
    given-names: Johan
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohanLindvall/logfmt"
url: "https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/JohanLindvall/logfmt"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - logfmt
  - Go
  - parser
  - logging
  - structured logging
  - zero allocation
  - SWAR
